# Data Sufficiency in Arithmetic

> Most data sufficiency questions are arithmetic wearing a disguise: ages,
> percentages, ratios, profit-loss, and speed. The master key is a count —
> unknowns versus independent equations — and this lesson drills it topic
> by topic with fully worked verdicts.

[important]
In arithmetic DS, a statement is sufficient when it supplies enough
*independent* constraints to pin every unknown in the stem. One linear
equation can never fix two unknowns — no matter how inviting the numbers.
[/important]

## 1. Why Arithmetic Dominates DS

